**How to implement.** The strict `X,Y` seam is deleted: the data proxy reads any attached file through its profile and its row selection, and reads a picked file for the wizard (001 §R 'The strict v1 `X,Y` path, whose parsers are reused as built-in import profiles'; the S9.2 brief: 'the fixed-schema attach in `ExperimentDataProxy`, `ExperimentDataStore.createFileBacked` and `ExperimentDataLoad` is replaced by attach-with-profile'; 001 §K 'One file → many experiments: split by a key column'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs`, after `validatedFor`: `type MappedPoints with member this.selectedBy (rows : DataRowSelection) : Result<MappedPoints, ExperimentDataError>`: `AllDataRows` keeps every point; `KeyedDataRows key` keeps the capture rows whose `experiment` label's text, the observations whose key and the mapped rows whose `keyOpt` equal it, a `SeriesPoints` being `MalformedDataFileErr` `an X,Y data file has no key column to select '<key>' by` (step 291's text, moved here), `ColumnPoints` none of whose rows holds a key `MalformedDataFileErr` `the import profile maps no key column to select '<key>' by`, and an empty selection `EmptyDataFileErr` `no row of the data file holds the key '<key>'`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataProxy.fs`: `ExperimentDataProxy` (`ExperimentDataProxy.fs:ExperimentDataProxy`, step 135) becomes `{ readPickedFile : FileName -> Result<LabFileSource, KitError>; attachDataFile : FileName -> Result<DataAttachment, KitError>; attachmentStatus : DataAttachment -> Result<DataAttachmentStatus, KitError>; readMapped : MappedAttachment -> Result<MappedPoints, ExperimentDataError> }`, still `[<ReferenceEquality>]`: `tryLoadIntensity` and `tryLoadEllipsometric` are deleted. The two new fields' one-line docs: a picked file's absolute name and bytes, read without touching the kit (the wizard's preview, step 308); and the points of an attachment's file read through its import profile, a built-in or the kit's, kept to its row selection. The module doc says so in one to three lines. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs`: `loadAndValidate` is `dataProxy.readMapped data` bound to `validatedFor (detectorKindOf library slots) experiment.scan` (step 304); step 291's name switch and key refusal are deleted from it, because the store resolves the name and `selectedBy` selects. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/ExperimentDataStore.fs`: its `<Compile>` line moves to directly after `LabFileImport.fs` (step 301), with no comment, because it reads through it. In `createFileBacked (kit : KitProxy)` (`ExperimentDataStore.fs:createFileBacked`, step 135): the picked file's read that `attachDataFile` does becomes one private function, and `readPickedFile file` answers its `{ file = file; content = <the bytes> }` or its `KitIoErr`, `attachDataFile` calling the same function; `readMapped data` reads `kit.readKitFile ()`, resolves `ChosenImportProfile.tryOfName kitFile.importProfiles data.profile` (step 300), `None` being `MalformedDataFileErr` `the import profile '<name>' is not available` (step 291's text, moved here), reads `kit.readDataFile data.attachment.path` (step 128), maps its `text` by `mapText` (step 303) and answers `selectedBy data.rows`; a `KitError` of either read is `MalformedDataFileErr` `could not read the data file '<path>' for the import profile '<name>': <e.describe>`, staying within the four-case channel. The private `DataFileKind` and `loadThrough` are deleted; the module doc says, in one to three lines, that the seam reads through the kit and the profile. (5) Every record expression that builds an `ExperimentDataProxy` replaces the two loads with `readMapped` and gains `readPickedFile`. `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`, `SolverHandoffView.fs`, `SolverHandoffWindow.fs` and `TableAndElementRotationView.fs` hold the proxy, build none and call `loadAndValidate` and `createFileBacked` as before, so nothing in them changes. Tests. `ImportProfileTests` gains `a row selection keeps every row or the rows of one key`: over test-local Phone ROI rows labelled `K1`, `K2`, `K1`, observations keyed `K1` and `K2`, and `Lab scan` rows keyed `K1` and `K2`, `AllDataRows` keeps each list whole and `KeyedDataRows (DataRowKey "K1")` keeps the two, one and one `K1` items; `K3` answers `EmptyDataFileErr`; a series answers `MalformedDataFileErr` naming the key; and rows with no key `MalformedDataFileErr`. `ExperimentDataProxyTests`: its mock, keyed by the attachment's path, answers `readMapped` with canned mapped points (`SeriesPoints` of the canned intensity series for an attachment mapped by `Intensity series`, of the ellipsometric one for `Ellipsometric series`) and `readPickedFile` with canned bytes; `a mock ExperimentDataProxy loads canned intensity and ellipsometric series through their exact signatures` is renamed `a mock ExperimentDataProxy reads canned mapped points and picked files through its exact signature` and `an unknown path yields a typed ExperimentDataError from both fields, never a throw` `an unknown path yields a typed ExperimentDataError, never a throw`, each asserting the same over the new fields; `loading data reads it through its import profile and refuses a profile or a row selection the X,Y files cannot serve` is renamed `loading data validates the points the attachment's profile maps`: step 288's one-axis experiment mapped by `Intensity series` answers the canned points validated, and by `Ellipsometric series` `DataUnitsMismatchErr`. `ExperimentDataStoreTests` (step 135), over `createFileBacked` of folder kits under the class's test directory, each folder now initialised through `initialiseKit` of a test-local kit file (step 125) before its files are placed, because `readMapped` reads the kit file: `createFileBacked round-trips a known intensity file through the step-34 parser`, `createFileBacked round-trips a known ellipsometric file through the step-34 parser` and `createFileBacked delegates parse semantics: an existing but empty file is the parser's EmptyDataFileErr` read through `readMapped` of the attachment mapped by `Intensity series` or `Ellipsometric series` over every row, keeping their names and assertions; `createFileBacked maps a missing file to a typed error from both fields, never a throw` is renamed `createFileBacked maps a missing file to a typed error through either X,Y profile, never a throw`; new `createFileBacked reads a data file through the kit's own profile and keeps the rows of its key`: a kit whose kit file holds `Lab scan` and a data file of rows keyed `K1`, `K2`, `K1` answers, for `KeyedDataRows (DataRowKey "K1")`, `ColumnPoints` of the two `K1` rows; new `createFileBacked refuses a profile the kit lacks and a key an X,Y file cannot select`: the profile `Nope` answers `MalformedDataFileErr` holding `the import profile 'Nope' is not available`, and an `Intensity series` attachment with `KeyedDataRows` `MalformedDataFileErr` holding `no key column`; new `createFileBacked reads a picked file whole without attaching it`: `readPickedFile` of a file written outside the kit answers its name and exact bytes, and the kit's paths are unchanged. `InverseConstructorTests`' `mockIntensity` and `mockEllipsometric` and `SolverHandoffWindowTests`' mocks answer `readMapped` with `SeriesPoints` of the series they answered, keyed by the attachment's path, and `readPickedFile` with an error; `ScrollExtentTests`' `noData` answers both new fields with an error. Every fact of the three classes keeps its assertions. After this step `git grep -n -E "tryLoadIntensity|tryLoadEllipsometric" -- Berreman/` finds nothing.

**Acceptance.** After the strict seam is deleted, `ExperimentDataProxy` MUST read an attachment through `readMapped` (its profile resolved from the built-ins and the kit file, its rows kept by `MappedPoints.selectedBy`) and a picked file through `readPickedFile`, and `git grep -n -E "tryLoadIntensity|tryLoadEllipsometric" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a row selection keeps every row or the rows of one key`, `createFileBacked reads a data file through the kit's own profile and keeps the rows of its key`, `createFileBacked refuses a profile the kit lacks and a key an X,Y file cannot select` and `createFileBacked reads a picked file whole without attaching it`, the count rising by 4, the renamed `a mock ExperimentDataProxy reads canned mapped points and picked files through its exact signature`, `an unknown path yields a typed ExperimentDataError, never a throw`, `loading data validates the points the attachment's profile maps` and `createFileBacked maps a missing file to a typed error through either X,Y profile, never a throw`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s30 invariants MUST pass.
